Let a platform's own API reach what its window keeps of a native view: `NativeView::platform_attachment`.

What: core's `NativeView` gains `platform_attachment(&self) -> &dyn Any`, the value the window's
`PlatformWindow::attach_native_view` returned. `NativeView::platform_attachment` (core) is how 0054's
`gpui_linux::NativeViewBuffers::of` reaches the view. Unused inside GPUI until 0054 (a public method, so no warning).

Why: the window's surface and frame commit are private to gpui_linux, so the app's way to commit buffers to its view
must come from gpui_linux, and it needs the view's platform state to do so.

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

